Reusability**\n\nThe potential use of `playbooks/deploy-ssh-key.yml` presents an opportunity to simplify user management. Creating a new, dedicated playbook might be a viable approach. This new playbook would create the user, set up passwordless SSH access, and deploy a known key.\n\n**Outlining Bootstrap Playbook Tasks**\n\nTo create the `koby-bowser-ansible` user with passwordless login, the `bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml` playbook will need to create the new user, manage user group membership, configure passwordless sudo, and deploy a specified key. This approach simplifies ongoing management.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml\n---\n- name: Bootstrap koby-bowser-ansible user with passwordless SSH & sudo\n  hosts: all\n  gather_facts: true\n  become: true\n  become_method: ansible.builtin.sudo\n  vars:\n    target_user: \"koby-bowser-ansible\"\n    local_pubkey_path: \"{{ lookup('env', 'HOME') }}/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub\"\n    ansible_ssh_common_args: \"-o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new\"\n\n  tasks:\n    - name: Verify local public key exists\n      ansible.builtin.stat:\n        path: \"{{ local_pubkey_path }}\"\n      register: pubkey_stat\n      delegate_to: localhost\n      become: false\n\n    - name: Fail if local public key does not exist\n      ansible.builtin.fail:\n        msg: \"Local public key not found at {{ local_pubkey_path }}.\"\n      when: not pubkey_stat.stat.exists\n\n    - name: Inspect effective sshd configuration\n      ansible.builtin.command: sshd -T\n      changed_when: false\n      register: sshd_config_raw\n\n    - name: Extract sshd AllowGroups if defined\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        sshd_allow_groups: >-\n          {{ (sshd_config_raw.stdout_lines\n              | select('match', '^allowgroups ')\n              | list | first | default('')\n              ).split()[1:] }}\n        sshd_auth_keys_pattern: >-\n          {{ ((sshd_config_raw.stdout_lines\n               | select('match', '^authorizedkeysfile ')\n               | list | first | default('authorizedkeysfile .ssh/authorized_keys')\n               ).split()[1:])[0] }}\n\n    - name: Create automation user\n      ansible.builtin.user:\n        name: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n        comment: \"Ansible Automation User\"\n        shell: /bin/bash\n        create_home: true\n        state: present\n\n    - name: Add automation user to sudo group\n      ansible.builtin.user:\n        name: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n        groups: sudo\n        append: true\n\n    - name: Add automation user to sshd AllowGroups if configured\n      ansible.builtin.user:\n        name: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n        groups: \"{{ item }}\"\n        append: true\n      loop: \"{{ sshd_allow_groups }}\"\n      when: sshd_allow_groups | length > 0\n\n    - name: Configure passwordless sudo in /etc/sudoers.d\n      ansible.builtin.copy:\n        content: \"{{ target_user }} ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\\n\"\n        dest: \"/etc/sudoers.d/{{ target_user }}\"\n        owner: root\n        group: root\n        mode: '0440'\n        validate: '/usr/sbin/visudo -cf %s'\n\n    - name: Retrieve target user passwd info\n      ansible.builtin.getent:\n        database: passwd\n        key: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n\n    - name: Determine user home and gid\n      ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n        target_home: \"{{ ansible_facts.getent_passwd[target_user][4] }}\"\n        target_gid: \"{{ ansible_facts.getent_passwd[target_user][2] }}\"\n\n    - name: Ensure ~/.ssh directory exists\n      ansible.builtin.file:\n        path: \"{{ target_home }}/.ssh\"\n        state: directory\n        owner: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n        group: \"{{ target_gid }}\"\n        mode: '0700'\n\n    - name: Deploy public key to user ~/.ssh/authorized_keys\n      ansible.posix.authorized_key:\n        user: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n        state: present\n        key: \"{{ lookup('file', local_pubkey_path) }}\"\n\n    - name: Deploy public key to centralized AuthorizedKeysFile if configured\n      when: \"'%u' in sshd_auth_keys_pattern\"\n      block:\n        - name: Resolve centralized authorized_keys path\n          ansible.builtin.set_fact:\n            central_auth_path: \"{{ sshd_auth_keys_pattern | replace('%u', target_user) | replace('%h', target_home) }}\"\n\n        - name: Ensure parent directory of centralized authorized_keys exists\n          ansible.builtin.file:\n            path: \"{{ central_auth_path | dirname }}\"\n            state: directory\n            owner: root\n            group: root\n            mode: '0755'\n\n        - name: Deploy key to centralized path\n          ansible.posix.authorized_key:\n            user: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n            path: \"{{ central_auth_path }}\"\n            key: \"{{ lookup('file', local_pubkey_path) }}\"\n            manage_dir: false\n            state: present\n\n        - name: Set strict permissions on centralized authorized_keys file\n          ansible.builtin.file:\n            path: \"{{ central_auth_path }}\"\n            owner: \"{{ target_user }}\"\n            group: \"{{ target_gid }}\"\n            mode: '0600'\n\n    - name: Report bootstrap completion\n      ansible.builtin.debug:\n        msg:\n          - \"Host: {{ inventory_hostname }}\"\n          - \"User {{ target_user }} successfully provisioned with passwordless sudo and SSH key access.\"\nEOF\nansible-lint /home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml\n","Cwd":"/home/koby/.ansible","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Create and lint bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml"}}]}
