{"step_index":337,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:23:52Z","thinking":"**Expanding Data Extraction Scope**\n\nConsideration for extracting additional data from KeePass entries beyond the initially targeted fields. Specifically, search for IP addresses within custom string fields like \"IP\", \"Host\", or \"Hostname\" by examining all string values.\n\nImportant: Eliminate the risk of storing passwords in the server pool file. Avoid storing potentially thousands of cleartext passwords in a plaintext YAML.\n\n\n**Validating Ansible Inventory Format**\n\nThe server pool data can be formatted as a valid Ansible inventory, storing server details like title, group, IP, and notes, but *not* passwords. The YAML structure was constructed to test this concept.\n\nA key challenge arises with ensuring valid Ansible host keys, specifically handling special characters, duplicate names, and missing IPs. A sanitation approach is necessary, and potentially having separate JSON/YAML files is an alternative.\n\n\n**Defining Playbook Functionality**\n\nThe playbook `/home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/kdbx-pool.yml` will manage the KeePass server pool. It has two modes: sync/build and search.\n\nThe sync mode builds the inventory from the KeePass database, prompting for the password to securely extract server data. The search mode takes a query and uses JSON search to find matching server entries, presenting the results.\n\n\n**Defining Script & Playbook Interactions**\n\nThe user might search directly with a query, or refresh/build the inventory, impacting the prompt for a password. If a query is provided, and the server pool exists, searching should not prompt for a password, but if it doesn't, it must first build and then search.  A separate shell helper script will also be created to avoid Ansible startup overhead.\n\n**Outlining Python Script Functionality**\n\nThe Python script `build_kdbx_pool.py` will handle building the inventory. It must accept optional command-line arguments, including the KeePass database path, output file paths (YAML and JSON), and an optional search query. The script will read the password from standard input and use it to export the KeePass data to XML, parse the XML, and output a valid Ansible inventory.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"cat << 'EOF' > /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nKeePass (.kdbx) Server Pool Builder & Search Engine\nExtracts server entries, IPs, logins, ports, and metadata from a KeePass database.\nGenerates both an Ansible-compatible inventory (YAML) and a fast-search cache (JSON).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport re\nimport json\nimport yaml\nimport subprocess\nimport argparse\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\nIP_REGEX = re.compile(\n    r'\\b(?:(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)\\.){3}(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|[01]?[0-9][0-9]?)\\b'\n)\nPORT_REGEX = re.compile(r':(\\d{2,5})\\b|port\\s*[:=]?\\s*(\\d{2,5})', re.IGNORECASE)\n\n# Filter out non-routable / netmask / broadcast IPs\nEXCLUDE_IPS = {'0.0.0.0', '255.255.255.255', '255.255.255.0', '255.0.0.0'}\n\n\ndef extract_servers_from_xml(xml_content):\n    root = ET.fromstring(xml_content)\n    servers = []\n\n    def parse_group(group_elem, current_path=''):\n        name_elem = group_elem.find('Name')\n        group_name = name_elem.text.strip() if (name_elem is not None and name_elem.text) else 'General'\n        group_path = f\"{current_path}/{group_name}\" if current_path else group_name\n\n        for entry in group_elem.findall('Entry'):\n            fields = {}\n            for s in entry.findall('String'):\n                k = s.find('Key')\n                v = s.find('Value')\n                if k is not None and k.text:\n                    fields[k.text.strip()] = (v.text.strip() if (v is not None and v.text) else '')\n\n            title = fields.get('Title', '').strip()\n            username = fields.get('UserName', '').strip()\n            url = fields.get('URL', '').strip()\n            notes = fields.get('Notes', '').strip()\n\n            # Collect all text to search for IPs & ports\n            all_text = \" \".join([title, url, notes] + list(fields.values()))\n            raw_ips = IP_REGEX.findall(all_text)\n            \n            # Deduplicate and filter out invalid/netmask IPs\n            ips = []\n            for ip in raw_ips:\n                if ip not in EXCLUDE_IPS and ip not in ips:\n                    ips.append(ip)\n\n            # Determine port\n            port = None\n            port_match = PORT_REGEX.search(f\"{url} {notes}\")\n            if port_match:\n                port_str = port_match.group(1) or port_match.group(2)\n                try:\n                    p = int(port_str)\n                    if 1 <= p <= 65535:\n                        port = p\n                except ValueError:\n                    pass\n\n            # Detect common protocol\n            protocol = 'ssh'\n            if 'rdp' in url.lower() or 'rdp' in notes.lower() or port == 3389:\n                protocol = 'rdp'\n            elif 'https' in url.lower() or port == 443:\n                protocol = 'https'\n            elif 'http' in url.lower() or port == 80:\n                protocol = 'http'\n\n            # Build record\n            if title or ips or username:\n                servers.append({\n                    'title': title or (ips[0] if ips else 'Unnamed'),\n                    'group': group_path,\n                    'ips': ips,\n                    'primary_ip': ips[0] if ips else None,\n                    'username': username,\n                    'port': port,\n                    'protocol': protocol,\n                    'url': url,\n                    'notes': notes,\n                    'custom_fields': {k: v for k, v in fields.items() if k not in {'Title', 'UserName', 'Password', 'URL', 'Notes'}}\n                })\n\n        for child_group in group_elem.findall('Group'):\n            parse_group(child_group, group_path)\n\n    root_group = root.find('Root')\n    if root_group is not None:\n        for g in root_group.findall('Group'):\n            parse_group(g)\n\n    return servers\n\n\ndef generate_ansible_inventory(servers):\n    \"\"\"Formats server list into an Ansible-compliant YAML inventory.\"\"\"\n    inventory = {\n        'all': {\n            'children': {\n                'kdbx_pool': {\n                    'hosts': {}\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    seen_hostnames = {}\n    for s in servers:\n        # Generate safe hostname key for Ansible\n        raw_name = s['title'] or s['primary_ip'] or 'host'\n        safe_name = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9_.-]', '_', raw_name).strip('_')\n        if not safe_name:\n            safe_name = f\"host_{s['primary_ip'].replace('.', '_')}\" if s['primary_ip'] else 'unknown_host'\n\n        # Ensure unique hostname\n        if safe_name in seen_hostnames:\n            seen_hostnames[safe_name] += 1\n            safe_name = f\"{safe_name}_{seen_hostnames[safe_name]}\"\n        else:\n            seen_hostnames[safe_name] = 1\n\n        host_entry = {}\n        if s['primary_ip']:\n            host_entry['ansible_host'] = s['primary_ip']\n        if s['username']:\n            host_entry['ansible_user'] = s['username']\n        if s['port']:\n            host_entry['ansible_port'] = s['port']\n        \n        # Metadata attributes\n        host_entry['kdbx_title'] = s['title']\n        host_entry['kdbx_group'] = s['group']\n        host_entry['kdbx_ips'] = s['ips']\n        host_entry['kdbx_protocol'] = s['protocol']\n        if s['notes']:\n            host_entry['kdbx_notes'] = s['notes'][:250]\n\n        inventory['all']['children']['kdbx_pool']['hosts'][safe_name] = host_entry\n\n    return inventory\n\n\ndef search_pool(servers, query):\n    \"\"\"Case-insensitive search across title, group, IPs, username, and notes.\"\"\"\n    q = query.lower().strip()\n    results = []\n    for s in servers:\n        haystack = \" \".join([\n            s['title'],\n            s['group'],\n            \" \".join(s['ips']),\n            s['username'],\n            s['url'],\n            s['notes']\n        ]).lower()\n        if q in haystack:\n            results.append(s)\n    return results\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"KeePass Server Pool Manager\")\n    parser.add_argument('--db', default='/home/koby/Documents/keePassXC/OMT_PFS.SYSTEME.ALL.kdbx', help='Path to .kdbx file')\n    parser.add_argument('--output-yaml', default='/home/koby/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.yml', help='Output Ansible inventory YAML')\n    parser.add_argument('--output-json', default='/home/koby/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json', help='Output JSON cache')\n    parser.add_argument('--search', help='Search query to filter servers')\n    parser.add_argument('--json-output', action='store_true', help='Output search results as JSON')\n    parser.add_argument('--sync', action='store_true', help='Force sync from KeePass DB')\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    # Search existing pool if --sync is not requested and pool files exist\n    if args.search and not args.sync and os.path.isfile(args.output_json):\n        with open(args.output_json, 'r') as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n        servers = data.get('servers', [])\n        matches = search_pool(servers, args.search)\n        if args.json_output:\n            print(json.dumps(matches, indent=2))\n        else:\n            print_search_results(matches, args.search)\n        return\n\n    # If syncing or pool missing: read KeePass DB\n    if not os.path.isfile(args.db):\n        # Fallback to Downloads if Documents path doesn't exist\n        fallback = '/home/koby/Downloads/OMT_PFS.SYSTEME.ALL.kdbx'\n        if os.path.isfile(fallback):\n            args.db = fallback\n        else:\n            print(f\"[ERROR] KeePass database not found at {args.db}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            sys.exit(1)\n\n    # Read master password from stdin\n    password = sys.stdin.read().rstrip('\\r\\n')\n    if not password:\n        print(\"[ERROR] Master password required via stdin.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    # Call keepassxc-cli export\n    cmd = ['keepassxc-cli', 'export', '-q', '-f', 'xml', args.db]\n    try:\n        proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdin=subprocess.PIPE, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)\n        stdout, stderr = proc.communicate(input=password)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[ERROR] Failed to execute keepassxc-cli: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        print(f\"[ERROR] Failed to decrypt KeePass database. Incorrect password or invalid database.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        if stderr:\n            print(stderr.strip(), file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(2)\n\n    # Parse XML\n    servers = extract_servers_from_xml(stdout)\n\n    # Create destination directories\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.output_yaml)), exist_ok=True)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.output_json)), exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Write JSON cache\n    payload = {\n        'metadata': {\n            'generated_at': datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n            'source_db': args.db,\n            'total_servers': len(servers),\n            'total_with_ip': sum(1 for s in servers if s['primary_ip'])\n        },\n        'servers': servers\n    }\n    with open(args.output_json, 'w') as f:\n        json.dump(payload, f, indent=2)\n\n    # Write Ansible Inventory YAML\n    inv_data = generate_ansible_inventory(servers)\n    with open(args.output_yaml, 'w') as f:\n        f.write(\"# Ansible Inventory generated automatically from KeePass database\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"# Source: {args.db}\\n\")\n        f.write(f\"# Total Servers: {len(servers)} | Updated: {datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()}\\n\\n\")\n        yaml.dump(inv_data, f, default_flow_style=False, sort_keys=False)\n\n    print(f\"[OK] Successfully built server pool: {len(servers)} total entries ({payload['metadata']['total_with_ip']} with IP addresses).\")\n    print(f\"     Ansible Inventory : {args.output_yaml}\")\n    print(f\"     Search Cache      : {args.output_json}\")\n\n    # If a search was requested alongside sync:\n    if args.search:\n        matches = search_pool(servers, args.search)\n        if args.json_output:\n            print(json.dumps(matches, indent=2))\n        else:\n            print_search_results(matches, args.search)\n\n\ndef print_search_results(matches, query):\n    C_RESET = \"\\033[0m\"\n    C_GREEN = \"\\033[0;32m\"\n    C_YELLOW = \"\\033[0;33m\"\n    C_BLUE = \"\\033[0;34m\"\n    C_BOLD = \"\\033[1m\"\n    C_CYAN = \"\\033[0;36m\"\n\n    print(f\"\\n{C_BOLD}=== [Search Results for '{query}': {len(matches)} match(es)] ==={C_RESET}\\n\")\n    if not matches:\n        print(f\"  {C_YELLOW}No matching servers found.{C_RESET}\\n\")\n        return\n\n    for idx, s in enumerate(matches, 1):\n        ips_str = \", \".join(s['ips']) if s['ips'] else \"No IP\"\n        user_str = s['username'] if s['username'] else \"None\"\n        port_str = f\"Port: {s['port']}\" if s['port'] else \"\"\n        proto_str = f\"[{s['protocol'].upper()}]\"\n\n        print(f\"  {C_BOLD}{idx:2d}. {C_GREEN}{s['title']}{C_RESET} {C_CYAN}{proto_str}{C_RESET}\")\n        print(f\"      {C_BOLD}IP(s)   :{C_RESET} {C_YELLOW}{ips_str}{C_RESET} {port_str}\")\n        print(f\"      {C_BOLD}User    :{C_RESET} {user_str}\")\n        print(f\"      {C_BOLD}Group   :{C_RESET} {C_BLUE}{s['group']}{C_RESET}\")\n        if s['notes']:\n            # Shorten notes for clean display\n            clean_notes = \" \".join(s['notes'].split())[:120]\n            print(f\"      {C_BOLD}Notes   :{C_RESET} {clean_notes}\")\n        print()\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\nEOF\nchmod +x /home/koby/.ansible/scripts/build_kdbx_pool.py\n","Cwd":"/home/koby/.ansible","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Create build_kdbx_pool.py script"}}]}
