{"step_index":365,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:30:28Z","thinking":"**Identifying Sensitive Data Patterns**\n\nThe internal convention uses `ssh30://` and `ssh22://` for specific connection schemes. Regular expression `ssh(\\d+)://` can be used to extract the ports automatically.\nAlso, the presence of \"port 30\" in notes or URLs must be considered as sensitive.\nNow, the password sanitization and masking engine's design requires identifying patterns needing scrubbing.\n\n\n**Developing Credential Sanitization Logic**\n\nThe initial focus is on defining regex patterns to identify and redact sensitive data within notes. Several common credential formats are considered, including \"user / password\", \"keyword: secret\", and variations. A Python function is being written to encapsulate this sanitization logic, utilizing regular expressions for pattern matching and replacement. Testing is underway with example inputs to ensure the function behaves as expected.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport re\n\ndef sanitize_notes(notes):\n    if not notes:\n        return ''\n    # User / Password pattern: e.g. root / secret, superuser / secret\n    t = re.sub(r'(?i)\\b([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+)\\s*/\\s*(\\S+)', r'\\1 / [PROTECTED]', notes)\n    # Password: secret, mdp: secret, pass: secret, sudo: secret\n    t = re.sub(r'(?i)\\b(password|passwd|pass|mdp|mot\\s*de\\s*passe|secret|sudo)\\s*[:=]\\s*(\\S+)', r'\\1: [PROTECTED]', t)\n    # User: secret\n    t = re.sub(r'(?i)\\b(root|admin|superuser)\\s*:\\s*(\\S+)', r'\\1: [PROTECTED]', t)\n    return t\n\nsamples = [\n    'root / cy/+v5Zp9IUu)u|jc6Xw,g*\\`q',\n    'Port 30 ssh\\nroot / 8&#JMl1Mwe0GyN',\n    'root / root2026',\n    'mdp: mySecret123',\n    'Password=TopSecret!',\n    'mot de passe : pass1234',\n    'Serveur Postfix port 30'\n]\n\nfor s in samples:\n    print('ORIGINAL:', repr(s))\n    print('MASKED  :', repr(sanitize_notes(s)))\n    print()\n\"","Cwd":"/home/koby/.ansible","WaitMsBeforeAsync":3000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Test password masking logic"}}]}
